{"id":"u-ac0643a8-ae06-4ee8-b6cc-0688944e419e","src":"community","title":"Judo & Grappling Strength 🥋","author":"Coach Greg Cooper","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/6Gyqpr-judo-and-grappling-strength","desc":"6-day workout plan for a high-level judo or grappling athlete prioritizing strength, power, and muscular density.\nExercises are judo/grappling-specific, balancing explosive lifts, functional hypertrophy, and recovery.\n\nKey Adjustments for Judo Performance\nTempo Work: Use slow eccentrics (3-4s) on accessory lifts (e.g., split squats) to boost tendon resilience.\nGrip Training: Add fat grips or towels to pulls/rows to mimic judogi gripping.\nCore Stability: Prioritize anti-rotation moves (e.g., Pallof presses) to enhance throwing power.\nIntensity Cycling: Deload every 4th week (reduce volume by 50%).\n\nNutrition & Recovery\nProtein: 200g/day (2.2g/kg) to support muscle repair.\nCarbs: 5-6g/kg on training days for energy.\nHydration: 4-5L daily (add electrolytes during rucking).\nSleep: 8-9 hours/night; 20-min naps post-training.\n\nThis plan balances strength, power, and judo-specific conditioning. Adjust weights weekly based on RPE (Rate of Perceived Exertion) to avoid overtraining.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Olympic Weightlifting","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":24,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-11-01T21:04:00.170Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Max Effort Lower - Squat Focus","Conditioning + Yoga","Max Effort Upper - Bench","Dynamic Effort Lower","Olympic Lifts + Upper Body","Conditioning + Yoga","Active Recovery"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":90,"x":5}]},{"n":"Power Clean","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"3x8 per leg \nTempo 3-1-2"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rotating Plank","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"3x12 per side"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Ruck","sets":[{"sec":3600,"rpe":6.5}]},{"n":"Yoga Flow","sets":[{"sec":1800,"rpe":6.5}],"note":"30 mins hip/shoulder mobility flow (e.g., pigeon pose, thread-the-needle)"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":90,"x":5}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":9,"x":5}],"note":"+20-30kg"},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Trap Bar Deadlift","sets":[{"r":2,"pct":60,"x":8}],"note":"8x2 @ 60% 1RM, Explosive Concentric"},{"n":"Single Leg Hip Thrust","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"3 x 12 per leg"},{"n":"Biking Intervals","sets":[{"sec":1800,"rpe":10}],"note":"Biking Intervals 1:1 Work:Rest Ratio"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Clean and Jerk","sets":[{"r":2,"pct":80,"x":5}]},{"n":"Push Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dumbbell Z-Press","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Farmer's Walk (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":40,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"3x40m Weight should test your grip"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Ruck","sets":[{"sec":3600,"rpe":6.5}]},{"n":"Yoga Flow","sets":[{"sec":1800,"rpe":6.5}],"note":"30 mins hip/shoulder mobility flow (e.g., pigeon pose, thread-the-needle)"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Cycling","sets":[{"sec":2700,"secHi":5400,"rpe":6}]},{"n":"Yoga Flow","sets":[{"sec":1800,"rpe":5}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":90,"x":5}]},{"n":"Power Clean","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"3x8 per leg \nTempo 3-1-2"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rotating Plank","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"3x12 per side"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Ruck","sets":[{"sec":3600,"rpe":6.5}]},{"n":"Yoga Flow","sets":[{"sec":1800,"rpe":6.5}],"note":"30 mins hip/shoul